<section id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hyper-parameters</h4>

<div id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further study the sensitivity of Nav-R1 to hyper-parameters on the RxR-CE Val-Unseen split. Tables <a href="#S8.T9" title="TABLE IX ‣ Hyper-parameters ‣ VIII Ablation Study ‣ Nav-R1: Reasoning and Navigation in Embodied Scenes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IX</span></a> report the ablation result.
For the KL penalty <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, too small values cause divergence from the reference policy, while too large values limit exploration.
The best trade-off is achieved at <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.02</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S8.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE IX: </span><span id="S8.T9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation on KL penalty <math id="S8.T9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Evaluation on RxR-CE Val-Unseen.</figcaption>
